 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(1)$ for a single static bounding box, as it involves a fixed number of vertices (24) and draw calls. For mesh grids, complexity is proportional to the number of divisions $O(\text{divs}^2)$. For tree topology, it is $O(N)$ where $N$ is the number of nodes [G].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ for static box (72 floats). Dynamic accumulation requires temporary storage for vertices before upload [S5, unofficial].
-- **Performance:** Very high, as it uses simple line primitives and minimal vertex data.
