 ## Background
-Bounding box drawing is a fundamental technique in computer graphics for visualizing object extents. In the context of volume rendering, it has been widely adopted in scientific visualization tools (e.g., ClearVolume-plus) and voxel engines (e.g., Elysian Outpost, voxel-engine) to aid user interaction and debugging [S2, S8, S9, unofficial]. The method relies on standard OpenGL line primitives and has been adapted for various integration contexts, including lattice and perspective plotting environments in R [S10].
